body: "## Observed exact-head CI failure (not a proven product regression)\n\nPR #150 head `12cb246b4c6f2df4fbe9f14d0a6348b21fd7df39`, [run 40407198356, Node22 job 121867905402](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40407198356/job/121867905402), Node22.23.3 on the hosted runner.\n\nThe job's `npm run release:check` test phase reports **2,070 tests, 2,070 passed, zero failures/cancellations** at22:09 UTC. The subsequent `bun run release:check` starts22:10 UTC. Its first reported failing test is `test/resolution-propagation.test.ts:317`, “different explicit choices already recorded by content merge retain exactly one dispute per unit”. It fails with:\n\n```text\nENOSPC: no space left on device, link\n$TMPDIR/pm-vcs-namespace-<synthetic-id>/destruction/<intent>.json.lock.<pid>.<nonce>.tmp\n-> $TMPDIR/pm-vcs-namespace-<synthetic-id>/destruction/<intent>.json.lock\n```\n\nLater tests repeatedly fail to create synthetic temporary directories with `ENOSPC`. The second test phase ends **2,061 tests / 1,311 passes / 750 failures**, followed by coverage threshold failures. Those cascaded errors are not evidence of750 independent product defects or meaningful coverage regressions.\n\nAt22:35 UTC the PR still has this exact head and Node22 remains failed; Node26 is still running, Windows launcher22/26 succeeded. No rerun, implementation edit or production operation was performed.\n\n## Expected / actual / impact\n\n[CI workflow at this head](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/12cb246b4c6f2df4fbe9f14d0a6348b21fd7df39/.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs the full npm and Bun gates. [Canonical phase6 acceptance](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/12cb246b4c6f2df4fbe9f14d0a6348b21fd7df39/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-phase6packs.toon) requires validated interruption/recovery behavior at unchanged thresholds.\n\nExpected: sequential release gates finish within the supported runner's resource budget and produce interpretable semantic/coverage results, while preserving fixture ownership and recovery evidence. Actual: the second gate encounters runner storage exhaustion and cascades into unrelated test failures, blocking exact-head certification.\n\nWhether the exhausted resource is bytes or inodes, and which fixture/coverage/workspace paths consume it, is **not established** by this log. Retained namespace records, repeated suite work, coverage output, or runner capacity are possibilities, not a diagnosed root cause. This is a hosted CI observation; no local reproduction or user-data loss is claimed.\n\n## Acceptance / regression protection\n\n- Capture bounded disk-byte/inode and relevant owned-fixture/coverage resource measurements around both full gates; identify the actual exhaustion source.\n- Make resource use or owned-fixture cleanup safe and bounded across repeated npm/Bun gates. Do not broadly remove foreign paths, discard required recovery data, skip semantic assertions, or lower coverage thresholds.\n- Add a repeatable regression/resource check tied to the measured cause; retain clear failure diagnostics before unrelated tests cascade.\n- Obtain clean full npm and Bun release gates on the same final immutable head, with explicit test/coverage results. Keep certification incomplete until then.\n\n## Duplicate / ownership checks\n\nChecked all153 current all-status issues/PRs (two pages), PR150 conversation/reviews/inline comments, and130 current canonical issue/chore/feature records. Existing #151 describes an older annotation teardown `ENOTEMPTY` failure, not this sequential-gate `ENOSPC`. The current [test-environment item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/12cb246b4c6f2df4fbe9f14d0a6348b21fd7df39/.agents/pm/issues/pm-vcs-testenv.toon) owns provenance/instrumentation isolation; no storage-exhaustion owner was found. No new PM ID is invented.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (3)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T02:05:38Z)\n>\n> ## Latest-head verification: sequential gates now succeed\n> \n> Checked unmerged PR #150 at `b412ea51aec1ef6da650818953bdc63bfde6139a` on 2026-10-27 at 02:05 UTC. This is hosted source-head verification, not npm publication or deployed-artifact certification; no issue closure is implied.\n> \n> - [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40413835438/job/121916160316) and [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40413835438/job/121916160730) both complete successfully. In each job, the full npm and subsequent Bun-invoked release gates each report **2,071 tests, 2,071 passes, zero failures**, and aggregate coverage is **100% across all four metrics**. The earlier sequential-gate ENOSPC cascade does not recur. Both Windows acceptance-launcher lanes also pass.\n> - The [cleanup commit](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/b412ea51aec1ef6da650818953bdc63bfde6139a) gives each full gate a separate `mktemp` directory under `RUNNER_TEMP`, exports it as `TMPDIR`, and retires that gate-owned directory on exit. This avoids accumulation between npm and Bun without changing production receipt retention.\n> - The added regression in [test/dependency-refresh-workflow.test.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/b412ea51aec1ef6da650818953bdc63bfde6139a/test/dependency-refresh-workflow.test.ts) exercises npm/Bun step scripts on success and exit 7, verifies native namespace receipts are inside the owned root, and preserves unrelated runner/outside sentinels. It is included in the successful hosted suites. Independent review inspected the exact workflow/test change and raw logs; it did not rerun the multi-hour full suites locally.\n> \n> Limits: the original failing runner's byte-versus-inode exhaustion and quantitative resource attribution remain unproven. These clean gates establish that the observed failure is superseded on this head, not that every resource-budget acceptance question is answered. Keep the final merged/published-artifact verification separate. Current head and issue comments were refreshed immediately before this update; no equivalent comment was present.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-31T18:57:37Z)\n>\n> Retained fixes: [b412ea5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/b412ea51aec1ef6da650818953bdc63bfde6139a) and [a06d928](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/a06d928bc64d60b5764e3e0a18735eed059e1e06), carried by `6dfc77631fdd528761aa7331f41588de481dde52`.\n> \n> Namespace audit receipts outlive individual synthetic repositories. Sharing their default scratch lifetime across sequential gates allowed those receipts to accumulate. Each npm/Bun gate now owns a separate scratch root and retires exactly that root on success or failure; production history is preserved. Byte/inode and owned-root diagnostics cannot override cleanup or the original exit status.\n> \n> The workflow regression passes in the current Node 22 selection and exercises success/failure plus unrelated sentinels. The completed diagnostic npm attempt used **3,336,840 KiB** of gate-owned scratch and removed that root after its unrelated memory-test failure. Its test result was 2,304/2,305, not a passing release gate. Earlier hosted verification on b412ea5 remains historical evidence; it does not certify this newer head. The original failing runner's byte-versus-inode exhaustion is still unproven.\n> \n> Current exact-head full npm/Bun acceptance is pending [CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41231846990). This comment does not close the issue.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T14:54:37Z)\n>\n> The per-gate owned scratch fix in b412ea5/a06d928 remains retained. [6a0d4b5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/commit/6a0d4b5d6253a1e2639c8af78fec34dff0fb557a) additionally routes benchmark disposable cleanup through caller-owned removal, avoiding persistent namespace receipts for disposable trees. Failed fragment restoration uses the same disposable path and preserves the primary failure. The existing durability/ownership retirement protocol is unchanged for persistent native state.\n> \n> Both cleanup regressions fail when their changed functions are reverted and pass after restoration. The isolated gate harness records bytes/inodes and removes its owned root on success/failure; the completed pack/GC, fragments, packed power-loss, Bun and Node 22 runs all removed those roots. Local counts are 70/70, 97/97, 3/3, 66/66 and 15/15 respectively. Historical byte-versus-inode exhaustion is not established by these measurements. No installer timeout was retried; an initial direct Bun invocation's five-second limit was corrected and its failed result is excluded.\n> \n> [Validation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/6a0d4b5d6253a1e2639c8af78fec34dff0fb557a/docs/validation/pr150-erasure-review-repair.md), [fresh CI](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/41318289087). Issue remains open for orchestrator verification."
